# Feature patch 0017 — erase loaded objects without rewriting their stream.
#
#   FPDFRejeb_PageEraseObjects(page, page_objects, count)
#       → overwrites the objects' own bytes with spaces in the original
#         content stream data — an image's `/Name Do`, or the `q` ... `Q`
#         pair around any other object — deactivates them and drops the
#         resources nothing references any more. Every other byte of the
#         page stays as it was, so nothing sharing the stream goes through
#         CPDF_PageContentGenerator. All or nothing.
#
#   Upstream files change, which the additive exports cannot avoid:
#     - CPDF_PageObject gains a SourceSpan, which CPDF_StreamContentParser
#       fills in: where the `Do` that painted an image ends, and the
#       innermost `q` ... `Q` pair painting the object and nothing else,
#       with the matrix in effect when it opened. The parser is the only
#       place that knows where an operator sits in the stream;
#       re-tokenizing later would have to guess which occurrence produced
#       which object.
#     - CPDF_PageContentGenerator::UpdateResourcesDict() becomes public so
#       unused entries can be dropped through the generator's own
#       shared-dictionary handling instead of a copy of it.
#
